  "aiOverview": {
    "content": "\"Boca\" most commonly refers to the Spanish word for \"mouth\" or an inlet, but is widely recognized as the name of the prestigious Boca Raton city/resort in Florida, the famed Boca Juniors football club, or popular restaurant brands. It also refers to Boca Foods, a manufacturer of plant-based burgers.Key \"Boca\" Topics:Boca Raton, Florida: A city in Palm Beach County known for its beaches, Mediterranean-style architecture, and high-end, luxury lifestyle.The Boca Raton Resort: An iconic, luxurious resort often referred to as \"The Boca,\" offering extensive amenities including a marina, golf, and spas.Cost of Living: Considered high; property prices, especially near the ocean, are high, attracting affluent residents.Boca Juniors (Club Atlético Boca Juniors): A renowned Argentine professional sports club based in Buenos Aires, famous for its football team. The team has a historic, constantly evolving badge design.Restaurants Named Boca:Boca (Cincinnati, OH): A high-end, European-influenced restaurant in Cincinnati.Boca Tacos y Tequila (Tucson, AZ): A well-known Mexican restaurant by Chef Maria Mazon.Boca (Florida): A brand with locations in Lake Mary, Winter Park, and Sarasota.Boca Foods: A brand of vegetarian/plant-based burgers and crumbles owned by Kraft Heinz.Definitions & Context:Spanish Definition: Boca means \"mouth.\" It is often used in geographic terms to describe an inlet or river mouth.Common Phrases: \"Quiete la boca\" translates to \"Keep your mouth shut\".",
